                <pb facs="0757" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg697"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Great Britain has accepted guarantee by Salvador of payment of indemnity by
                    Nicaragua in London within a fortnight; and so soon as Nicaragua accepts and so
                    informs British admiral he is instructed to leave Corinto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
